# One value with several meanings, in lambda plus merge: scored points of
# the label-free family where a reverse index of a knowledge base must give one
# term more than one meaning (a term can have several meanings: \z. \s. z
# is zero, and nil, and true). The
# reduction series poses the same program with its answer read by Scott
# case analysis (contest_reduction_meanings.pl); these points pose it to
# is_identity, the count compared with a claimed numeral.
#
# THE VALUE is \t. \f. t: the Church true, and the Scott unary zero
# \z. \s. z, one term. The program let binds it once as True and uses
# that one variable in both meanings:
# - as a Boolean: is_even returns it, the count's choice applies it, and
#   the unary equality answers it;
# - as the unary zero: n is doubled up from it at run time, the input
#   numerals are built from it, the count starts from it, and the claimed
#   numeral is built on it.
#
# THE PROGRAM counts the even numbers among 0, 1, ..., n - 1, with the
# is_even, count and upto of contest_reduction_meanings.pl, and compares
# the count with a claimed unary numeral:
# - double = \self. \x. x True (\p. successor (successor (self self p))),
#   and n = 2^k is double applied k times to one, so that the program
#   stays small (a literal of depth n made the translation take 7588 ms
#   at n = 1024 in the reduction series);
# - equal = \self. \a. \b. a (b True (\_. False))
#   (\p. b False (\q. self self p q)), the unary equality;
# - the test is equal (count (upto n True) True) claimed, the Church
#   Boolean of count = claimed. The count of evens below 2^k is 2^(k-1),
#   and the claimed numeral is double applied k - 1 times to one, or its
#   successor for the wrong claim.
# is_even of k takes k steps, so the program takes O(n^2) steps.
#
# THE POINTS: n = 256, 512 and 1024, and a wrong claim at 512, the count
# plus one, which the equality refutes only after reading every
# successor of the count.
#
# READINGS (2026-09-29, CPU 2 under contest_limited.sh, point_claims/2, a
# fresh process per reading, the family's limits):
# - weak_head: 256 in 4030 ms; 512, its wrong claim and 1024 stopped;
# - tabling(weak_head): 256, 512, the wrong 512 and 1024 in 285, 581, 583
#   and 976 ms, the tables sharing is_even of each numeral with the next.
# These points are not a frontier for tabling: they give a reverse index
# a value it must read in two meanings, in the scored suite.
# LIMITS: the family's, 10 s, 256 MB, 256 MB.
#
# TARGET ALGORITHMS, the specific known algorithms the problem targets, each
# with its prior work:
# - one shared representation for a term with several meanings, as
#   hash-consing shares equal terms: J.-C. Filliâtre, S. Conchon, Type-Safe
#   Modular Hash-Consing, ML Workshop 2006, doi:10.1145/1159876.1159880.
# - tabled evaluation, which shares is_even of each numeral with the next:
#   W. Chen, D. S. Warren, Tabled Evaluation with Delaying for General Logic
#   Programs, J. ACM 1996, doi:10.1145/227595.227597.

#   count_point(?Point, ?Exponent, ?Extra): n = 2^Exponent, the claim
#   2^(Exponent - 1) + Extra.
#
# Each text is from_cbor of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes,
# imported from corpora/library/text/cbor. Each number is from_cbor of an
# integer literal, a Scott integer, imported from corpora/library/integer/cbor.
# FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "text") "cbor")
λ text_from_cbor _ _ _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. text_from_cbor λx. x)
λ text
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "integer") "cbor")
λ integer_from_cbor _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. integer_from_cbor λx. x)
λ integer
. export
λ
. cons
  (λ_count_point. _count_point (text "merge_even_count_two_hundred_fifty_six") (integer 8) λ. integer 0)
λ
. cons
  (λ_count_point. _count_point (text "merge_even_count_five_hundred_twelve") (integer 9) λ. integer 0)
λ
. cons
  ( λ _count_point
    . _count_point (text "merge_even_count_five_hundred_twelve_wrong") (integer 9) λ. integer 1
  )
λ
